Journey: Home rating scenario <caseId> (<note>)
Id: quote-matrix-home
Tags: @portal @rating @data-driven @regression
Role: policyholder
Risk: 4
Requirements: RATE-1, RATE-3
Description: One run per row of the underwriting team's workbook (sheet "Home", runFlag Y only).

Log in
Run journey "quote-on-portal" with product="<product>", sumInsured=<sumInsured>, regionLabel="<regionLabel>", riskAge=<riskAge>, noClaimsYears=<noClaimsYears> and store the result as rated
Run journey "expected-premium" with product="<product>", sumInsured=<sumInsured>, region="<region>", riskAge=<riskAge>, noClaimsYears=<noClaimsYears> and store the result as expected
Expect ${rated.premium.totalPremium} == ${expected.total}
Expect ${rated.premium.netPremium} == ${expected.net}
Expect ${rated.premium.tax} == ${expected.tax}
If ${expected.net} == 150 then
  # Data-dependent branch: the minimum premium rule, not the rating table, decided this one
  Expect ${expected.loaded} - ${expected.discount} < 150
End
Call API "GET ${API_URL}/v1/quotes/${rated.quoteRef}" as broker and store as stored
Expect response stored "$.premium.totalPremium" equals "${expected.total}"
Expect response stored "$.product" equals "<product>"

Examples: from data "data/rating-matrix.xlsx" sheet "Home" where runFlag = Y
